Customer Demographics Analysis

🎯 Objective
This section explores customer purchasing behavior across different demographic segments, focusing on age groups and household composition. 
The goal is to identify which customer segments generate the highest sales and how spending behavior varies across household types.

📊 1. Sales Contribution by Age Group
Methodology
Total sales were aggregated by customer age group to evaluate which demographic segments contribute most to overall revenue.

(household_sales_demo
    .groupby("AGE_DESC", observed = False)
    .agg({"SALES_VALUE" : "sum"})
    .plot.bar()
)

Insight
Middle-aged customer groups contribute the highest share of total sales, indicating stronger purchasing activity and higher revenue contribution from these segments.

🌡️ 2. Spending Behavior by Age & Household Type
Methodology
A pivot table was used to analyze average sales across combinations of age groups and household composition. 
This enables a multi-dimensional view of customer spending behavior.

household_sales_demo.pivot_table(
    index=["AGE_DESC"],
    columns=["HH_COMP_DESC"],
    values="SALES_VALUE",
    aggfunc="mean",
    margins=True,
    observed=False
).style.background_gradient(cmap="RdYlGn", axis=None)

Insight
Households with children tend to exhibit higher average spending levels, particularly in the 35–54 age groups. 
This suggests that both age and household composition significantly influence purchasing behavior.



